Z||000001||fiero56||02-02-2001||03:55 PM||||Rent a press and do 'em yourself for free. AZ rents 'em for $120, and once you return the press, they refund your money.||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||02-02-2001||04:33 PM||||only the lower front ball joints need pressing in.  i bought a pair from carquest for $34, and they installed them.<P>of course they were drilling out the old ball joints, and doing some cleanup work on all my control arms for $65!<P>check with them, b4 you do anything!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000003||Notchit||02-02-2001||05:08 PM||||How can you tell if the ball joints need to be pressed?<P>------------------<BR>Seein Red<BR>'85 Fiero GT<BR>ICQ#: 56708070<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Outside_side2(sml2).jpg"> <BR>_________________________||||reg||4
Z||000004||mrfiero||02-02-2001||09:16 PM||||The pressed on ones have a serated edge all the way around the butt of the joint (the control arm has the same serated edge) and has no provision for rivets/bolts.  <P>I would say that 99.9% of all cars have pressed on lower balljoints.  The uppers are held in place by rivets or bolts/nuts.....early Fieros have bolted on upper balljoints, while the '88s were riveted from the factory (replaement '88 uppe are bolted on whch requires drilling out the original rivets).<P>With the ball joint press it is a simple procedure that takes only a few minutes.  The hard part is removing the old balljoint (I use a big sledge hammer).  Some early Fieros ha the lower baljoint tack welded in place oo, so you might have to grind off these welds first.||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||02-02-2001||09:56 PM||||I don't have any valuable information to contribute, I just wanted to say that the title of this thread sounded dirty and vaguely disturbing. That is all.||||reg||6
Z||000006||mshill||02-03-2001||12:17 AM||||I had mine done for $10 each at a local machine shop that  just happened to be right next to a Napa Autoparts store.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cooter||02-03-2001||12:29 AM||||On my 88, I borrowed the ball joint/tie rod press from the Carport parts store. The manager is a friend and he did not charge the rental/return fee. I did not think it would work, but with an impact wrench and a lot of PB Blaster they came out and were replaced in about 30 minutes. Getting the old rubber bushings out- now that is a different story!||||reg||1
